Z||000000||Hank is Here||04-30-2001||04:47 PM||||This is completely theoretical, or better put for shitz and giggles<BR>Since basically every other GM engine has been swapped into a Fiero has anyone ever heard of swapping in a Saturn 3000cc engine in the new L series?  Is this engine an Opel engine or a Saturn design?  It lists 182 HP, 190 ft/lbs,  24v DOHC <BR>Which bolt pattern would this be the standard FWD one like in the Fiero or the other weird one like on the Q4?  <BR>I am not going to attempt this swap but it should be a good conversation piece.  <P>I did run a quick search but found nothing.<P>Hank is Here (Mark)  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||04-30-2001||05:37 PM||||Just did a little more snooping around the net.  This is a European engine.  Here in the states it is also used in the Caddy Catera, except it is rated at 200 HP rather than 182 in the Saturn.  The Catera is RWD while the Saturn is FWD.  So what is you took a Caddy engine and mated it to the Saturn tranny?  you would have  200HP and 192 ft/lbs from only 3 liters, but I would think the computer would be he!! to work with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||05-01-2001||02:31 PM||||bump...  no one has any opinion on 200hp from 3L?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||05-01-2001||02:43 PM||||It would be a nice engine for a fiero but the wiring would probably be a nightmare..<BR>but, anybody who has swapped a tdc or fwd 3.4 or quad 4 would have no problems with it.<BR>but I would chose a 3.4 fwd or the tdc before the saturn engine.<P>"those saturns......they're plastic"<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||05-01-2001||03:39 PM||||The wiring would not be a problem at all, just toss the Saturn/Cadillac ECM and use an aftermarket fuel management system. a guy has been trying to sell a Catera engine and trans on Ebay, never gets any bids <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=579661841&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=579661841&r=0&t=0</A> <BR>The starter is on the wrong side, the air inlet is on the wrong end, who knows what other problems you may run into. I guess if you could do it, you'd have "the Fiero that Zigs".||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||05-01-2001||05:40 PM||||Anyone but me notice the dual throttle bodies on that sucker...?||||reg||1
Z||000006||ray b||05-01-2001||07:28 PM||||is the 3.0 and 3.5 same block desine? olds 3.5 is that same as isusu 3.5 al truck motor? thats rated at 240 hp in new 01 model.<BR>saturn motor looks diffrent with intake rapped around out side of motor long rams that stick out 2 to 3 inchs pass valve covers<BR>in front and rear and may be a clearance promlem in a fiero[firewall]. caddy looks like a better fit in 3.0sv-6 swaps. what does the 3.5 look like olds or isusu???<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
